ATTRIBUTION

Fuse Energy provides no public API. What is known about it was worked out by
other people first, and this project rests on two pieces of prior research.

    LionZXY/FuseEnergyApi  (December 2024, no licence stated)
    https://github.com/LionZXY/FuseEnergyApi

A Kotlin client, and the earliest public reverse-engineering of this API that
we are aware of. It established the API base, the token refresh endpoint and
its retry-on-401 behaviour, and the customer / property / readings shape. It
records the OTP issue endpoint but could not complete a sign-in without the
mobile app, and falls back to intercepting the token from a rooted handset.

    simonsolts/fuse-homeassistant  (AGPL-3.0, May 2026)
    https://github.com/simonsolts/fuse-homeassistant

Worked out the parts that let an integration authenticate itself and stay
correct over time: that signing in takes two calls and only the second
dispatches the SMS, the version header the website expects, the endpoints as
they now stand, and how the hourly figures settle in the days after they first
appear.

Both informed this project and the credit for that research is theirs.

This acknowledgement is given because it is deserved, not because a licence
compels it. No code from either project was copied into this one: both are
public, and a file-by-file comparison shows no shared implementation. What is
shared is knowledge about a third party's API -- endpoints, headers and
protocol behaviour -- which is not itself anyone's to license.
